  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to Maine total $1.2B for FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 68.8% year over year. Federal buyers issued 6,575 awards so far, with an average award size of $186K. The Department of Defense dominates buying in the state, accounting for $1.1B of obligations. Ship building and repair work and health insurance payments lead industry spending, with $480M and $433M respectively. Year-to-date vendor receipts are concentrated: BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION received $470M and MARTINS POINT HEALTH CARE INC received $433M. Historical context shows higher annual totals in recent years: FY21 was $2.4B, FY22 was $2.7B, FY23 was $3.7B, FY24 was $3.7B, and FY25 was $3.9B. Current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal spending in Maine right now?",
        "body": "Spending is highly concentrated by buyer and industry. The Department of Defense accounts for $1.1B of the $1.2B total. Ship Building and Repairing and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers together account for $480M and $433M respectively. A small number of vendors capture most dollars, with the top two firms alone receiving $470M and $433M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date totals $1.2B, which is lower than each full prior year listed. FY21 was $2.4B, FY22 was $2.7B, FY23 was $3.7B, FY24 was $3.7B, and FY25 was $3.9B. Obligations are down 68.8% year over year, reflecting that current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date. Award volume remains sizable at 6,575 awards with an average award size of $186K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Maine?",
      "a": "Federal contract obligations to Maine total $1.2B in FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 68.8% year over year. Federal buyers have issued 6,575 awards so far, and the average award size is $186K. Historical full-year totals were $2.4B in FY21, $2.7B in FY22, $3.7B in FY23, $3.7B in FY24, and $3.9B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Maine?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, with $1.1B in obligations. Other top buying agencies are the Department of Labor with $28M, the Department of Veterans Affairs with $24.2M, and the Department of Agriculture with $18.4M. The General Services Administration, Department of Homeland Security, Department of the Interior, Department of Health and Human Services, Department of Justice, and Department of Energy follow with $10.3M, $7.4M, $4.9M, $2.3M, $1.6M, and $1.3M respectively."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Maine?",
      "a": "BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION and MARTINS POINT HEALTH CARE INC are the largest federal contractors in Maine, with $470M and $433M in obligations respectively. Other sizable vendors include 381 CONSTRUCTORS with $63.9M, MOHAWK NORTHEAST INC with $24.4M, and CIANBRO CORPORATION with $18.6M. The next vendors listed received $16.1M, $10.6M, $10.6M, $9.2M, and $8.9M respectively."
